{"audit_run_id":"audit:69211f61a37f48efb9657891d1df006c","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":80,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Sixty individual set-yoghurt cups, filled on one day from a single homogenised,"},{"end_column":71,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"heat-treated milk lot. Thirty cups were inoculated with a conventional"},{"end_column":77,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"thermophilic starter and thirty with an exopolysaccharide-producing starter,"},{"end_column":79,"end_line":8,"start_column":1,"start_line":8,"text":"then incubated and chilled under identical conditions. Each cup was opened and"},{"end_column":59,"end_line":9,"start_column":1,"start_line":9,"text":"measured individually after seven days of chilled storage."},{"end_column":75,"end_line":11,"start_column":1,"start_line":11,"text":"**One row is one cup.** Each row carries the cup's identifier, the starter"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":12,"start_column":1,"start_line":12,"text":"culture it was inoculated with, and that cup's value for each of the eight"},{"end_column":76,"end_line":13,"start_column":1,"start_line":13,"text":"declared outcome variables. There are 60 rows plus a header row, 30 cups in"},{"end_column":34,"end_line":14,"start_column":1,"start_line":14,"text":"each group, and no missing cells."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":18,"start_column":1,"start_line":18,"text":"The eight outcome columns appear in the declared outcome order fixed in the"},{"end_column":12,"end_line":19,"start_column":1,"start_line":19,"text":"trial plan."},{"end_column":49,"end_line":21,"start_column":1,"start_line":21,"text":"| # | Column | What it is | Unit | Reported to |"},{"end_column":49,"end_line":22,"start_column":1,"start_line":22,"text":"|---|--------|------------|------|-------------|"},{"end_column":142,"end_line":23,"start_column":1,"start_line":23,"text":"| 1 | `cup_id` | Cup identifier, `cup_` plus a zero-padded three-digit serial number (`cup_001` to `cup_060`). One per cup, unique. | — | — |"},{"end_column":188,"end_line":24,"start_column":1,"start_line":24,"text":"| 2 | `starter_culture` | Group column. Exactly two distinct values: `conventional` for the conventional thermophilic starter, `eps` for the exopolysaccharide-producing starter. | — | — |"},{"end_column":81,"end_line":25,"start_column":1,"start_line":25,"text":"| 3 | `ph_24h` | pH of the cup 24 hours after filling. | pH units | 2 decimals |"},{"end_column":139,"end_line":26,"start_column":1,"start_line":26,"text":"| 4 | `titratable_acidity_pct` | Titratable acidity at day seven, expressed as percent lactic acid by mass. | % lactic acid | 2 decimals |"},{"end_column":162,"end_line":27,"start_column":1,"start_line":27,"text":"| 5 | `syneresis_pct` | Syneresis (whey drainage) at day seven, as percent by mass of the cup contents. Lower means less whey released. | % by mass | 1 decimal |"},{"end_column":133,"end_line":28,"start_column":1,"start_line":28,"text":"| 6 | `gel_firmness_n` | Gel firmness at day seven from a penetration test, as the peak force recorded. | newtons (N) | 2 decimals |"},{"end_column":138,"end_line":29,"start_column":1,"start_line":29,"text":"| 7 | `apparent_viscosity_pa_s` | Apparent viscosity at day seven, measured at a fixed shear rate. | pascal seconds (Pa·s) | 2 decimals |"},{"end_column":157,"end_line":30,"start_column":1,"start_line":30,"text":"| 8 | `water_holding_capacity_pct` | Water-holding capacity at day seven, as a percentage. Higher means the gel retains more of its water. | % | 1 decimal |"},{"end_column":133,"end_line":31,"start_column":1,"start_line":31,"text":"| 9 | `lab_count_log10_cfu_g` | Viable lactic acid bacteria count at day seven. | log10 colony-forming units per gram | 2 decimals |"},{"end_column":177,"end_line":32,"start_column":1,"start_line":32,"text":"| 10 | `sensory_smoothness_score` | Sensory smoothness: the trained panel's mean rating for that cup on a 1 to 9 scale, with 9 the smoothest. | scale points (1–9) | 1 decimal |"},{"end_column":75,"end_line":36,"start_column":1,"start_line":36,"text":"- Values are fixed and committed in the CSV. They are not generated at run"},{"end_column":24,"end_line":37,"start_column":3,"start_line":37,"text":"time by the analysis."},{"end_column":77,"end_line":38,"start_column":1,"start_line":38,"text":"- Each value is rounded to the precision the corresponding instrument or the"},{"end_column":60,"end_line":39,"start_column":3,"start_line":39,"text":"sensory panel would report, as listed in the table above."},{"end_column":71,"end_line":40,"start_column":1,"start_line":40,"text":"- The two primary product-quality outcomes named in the trial plan are"},{"end_column":78,"end_line":41,"start_column":3,"start_line":41,"text":"`syneresis_pct` and `gel_firmness_n`. The other six outcome columns are the"},{"end_column":31,"end_line":42,"start_column":3,"start_line":42,"text":"declared secondary outcomes."},{"end_column":76,"end_line":43,"start_column":1,"start_line":43,"text":"- The two groups overlap on every outcome; scatter is at the level expected"},{"end_column":46,"end_line":44,"start_column":3,"start_line":44,"text":"for replicate cups drawn from one milk lot."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:645d6732dd3a2b2bf2ff","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:3e8dff65b68da029e8d03baa6e87f517de1dd8feac5f8382ab93021654dc1ce4","end_line":44,"locator":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md:1-44","path":"DATA_DESCRIPTION.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
{"audit_run_id":"audit:69211f61a37f48efb9657891d1df006c","completed_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","coverage_status":"covered","emitted_record_refs":[],"extensions":{"x-candidate-spans":[{"end_column":99,"end_line":3,"start_column":1,"start_line":3,"text":"This study compares the two groups recorded in the `starter_culture` column of `yoghurt_cups.csv`."},{"end_column":223,"end_line":4,"start_column":1,"start_line":4,"text":"The pre-declared outcome family, in this fixed order, is: ph_24h, titratable_acidity_pct, syneresis_pct, gel_firmness_n, apparent_viscosity_pa_s, water_holding_capacity_pct, lab_count_log10_cfu_g, sensory_smoothness_score."},{"end_column":85,"end_line":5,"start_column":1,"start_line":5,"text":"Each outcome is compared between the two groups. The named outcomes form one outcome"},{"end_column":88,"end_line":6,"start_column":1,"start_line":6,"text":"family; per-outcome comparisons over this family require complete-family control of the"},{"end_column":45,"end_line":7,"start_column":1,"start_line":7,"text":"family-wise error from multiple comparisons."}],"x-expected-count-method-declarations":[],"x-explicit-directional-claims":[],"x-explicit-expected-count-sensitivities":[],"x-explicit-quantitative-claims":[]},"opaque_constructs":[],"parser_disagreement":null,"parser_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","parser_result_id":"parser-result:e3a0ceaa2606fdaa4c39","parser_version":"0.2.0","provenance":{"actor":{"actor_id":"parser:markdown-inventory","actor_kind":"parser"},"created_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","method":"static_inventory","tool":"sc-referee","tool_version":"0.3.0"},"record_type":"parser_result","schema_version":"0.21.0","source_ref":{"content_digest":"sha256:f4ea6c9b44745e454f082d4f3963afdcac04124124bbb15739720bbecf1860bd","end_line":7,"locator":"PROTOCOL.md:1-7","path":"PROTOCOL.md","source_kind":"file_span","start_line":1},"started_at":"2026-07-27T20:00:00Z","state":"parsed","syntax_issues":[]}
